hints:
push_front is two moves: the new node takes the old chain, then the list takes the new node.
```cpp
auto n = std::make_unique<Node>();
n->value = v;
n->next = std::move(head_);
head_ = std::move(n);
++size_;
```

Traverse with a raw, non-owning pointer and never copy a `unique_ptr`:
```cpp
Node* cur = head_.get();
while (cur) { /* cur->value */ cur = cur->next.get(); }
```
For `push_back`, walk until `cur->next` is empty and move the new node into that slot (or into `head_` if the list is empty). For `pop_front`: `head_ = std::move(head_->next);` frees the old head.

reverse: peel the head off, point it at the reversed prefix, repeat.
```cpp
std::unique_ptr<Node> prev;
while (head_) {
    auto next = std::move(head_->next);   // detach the rest
    head_->next = std::move(prev);        // old head now points at the reversed part
    prev = std::move(head_);              // reversed part grows by one
    head_ = std::move(next);              // advance
}
head_ = std::move(prev);
```
